# Shell scripts MUST keep LF endings.
#
# This repo is authored on Windows, where git's autocrlf converts LF to CRLF
# on checkout. A .sh file with CRLF endings fails on macOS and Linux with:
#
#     bash: ./scripts/render_sql.sh: /usr/bin/env bash^M: bad interpreter
#
# Learners run these from their own laptops, so this is not hypothetical.
*.sh    text eol=lf

# Python and SQL are read by Glue (Linux) and by Redshift. Keep them LF for
# the same reason, and so diffs stay clean across the team's mixed machines.
*.py    text eol=lf
*.sql   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf

# CSV seed data: LF, so the row counts the Glue jobs assert against do not
# shift with a stray carriage return in the last column.
*.csv   text eol=lf
